  "content": {
    "text": "00:00 Speaker A\nMicron shares are on a record again today, Dan. Um, they now also just this morning announced a new partnership with Anthropic. They're going to be providing chips to them and they're out with earnings this week.\n00:12 Dan\nYeah, the uh deal with Anthropic is interesting. It's they don't mention how much, uh but they do say that they will be uh in a supply agreement for uh both memory and storage. So that's, you know, memory would be their RAM uh and storage would be storage. Um, but that that is interesting. Uh they also say that uh Micron will start uh using Anthropic's technology and then that they'll have some work together where they try to come up with some new efficiencies for for memory in the the long-term. Uh but I think most people are interested in the the supply uh agreement there. And then yeah, I mean, we're going to get Micron's earnings this week. Basically providing, you know, another look at uh the overall AI industry and and the health of it. And this is supposed to be a a big report for Micron. Uh the revenue is supposed to come in at 35.5 billion, that would be up 281% year-over-year. Uh that's from 9.3 billion in the same uh quarter last year. DRAM, that's that uh what we call memory. Uh that's going to contribute 27.5 billion to that total. Uh that's up 288% and then storage would be uh 7.7 billion, again up 256%. Then I just want to talk about gross margins real quick. They're supposed to come in at 110% uh up from 97% last quarter. So, you know, they really are kind of on a tear here if we get to the the numbers to come in uh as this uh Bloomberg consensus out uh analysis, consensus comes uh in, that would be massive for them.\n01:54 Speaker A\nYeah, I'm just looking at the net income estimate at 23.48 billion. That's a cool 977%.\n02:05 Dan\nNo big deal.\n02:06 Speaker A\nIt's, yeah. So this is why when everybody talks about, you know, the the rally here, a lot of folks are saying, a lot of analysts we've spoken to have said it is indeed backed up by the incredible growth. You know, we'll see what it actually looks like when the numbers come out.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "00:00 Speaker A",
      "Micron shares are on a record again today, Dan. Um, they now also just this morning announced a new partnership with Anthropic. They're going to be providing chips to them and they're out with earnings this week.",
      "00:12 Dan",
      "Yeah, the uh deal with Anthropic is interesting. It's they don't mention how much, uh but they do say that they will be uh in a supply agreement for uh both memory and storage. So that's, you know, memory would be their RAM uh and storage would be storage. Um, but that that is interesting. Uh they also say that uh Micron will start uh using Anthropic's technology and then that they'll have some work together where they try to come up with some new efficiencies for for memory in the the long-term. Uh but I think most people are interested in the the supply uh agreement there. And then yeah, I mean, we're going to get Micron's earnings this week. Basically providing, you know, another look at uh the overall AI industry and and the health of it. And this is supposed to be a a big report for Micron. Uh the revenue is supposed to come in at 35.5 billion, that would be up 281% year-over-year. Uh that's from 9.3 billion in the same uh quarter last year. DRAM, that's that uh what we call memory. Uh that's going to contribute 27.5 billion to that total. Uh that's up 288% and then storage would be uh 7.7 billion, again up 256%. Then I just want to talk about gross margins real quick. They're supposed to come in at 110% uh up from 97% last quarter. So, you know, they really are kind of on a tear here if we get to the the numbers to come in uh as this uh Bloomberg consensus out uh analysis, consensus comes uh in, that would be massive for them.",
      "01:54 Speaker A",
      "Yeah, I'm just looking at the net income estimate at 23.48 billion. That's a cool 977%.",
      "02:05 Dan",
      "No big deal.",
      "02:06 Speaker A",
      "It's, yeah. So this is why when everybody talks about, you know, the the rally here, a lot of folks are saying, a lot of analysts we've spoken to have said it is indeed backed up by the incredible growth. You know, we'll see what it actually looks like when the numbers come out."
    ],
